    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0135" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg645"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Elsey Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Thomas</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-02-22T16:55:00-04:00">February 22, 1948—4:55 p. m.
                            EST.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Blue 4. Your working draft of recommended basic
                        position<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/> for Security Council discussion
                    Tuesday received. I approve in principle this basic position. I want to make it
                    clear, however, that nothing should be presented to Security Council that could
                    be interpreted as a recession on our part from the position we took in the
                    General Assembly.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d52-f2"/> Send final draft of Austin’s
                    remarks for my consideration.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="1" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#pg637">p. 637</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f2" n="2" xml:id="d52-f2-content">
                <p>On November 29, 1947, i.e., in support of the partition of Palestine into Jewish
                    and Arab states.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
